    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Released in 1999, Supergrass is the third studio album by the British rock band Supergrass and the group’s self-titled statement of maturity after the exuberant rush of I Should Coco. Often nicknamed the “X-Ray” album because of its cover art, it leans into polished Britpop and alternative rock, balancing energetic guitar pop with more expansive arrangements and a slightly more reflective mood. Tracks such as “Pumping on Your Stereo” helped anchor the record’s commercial appeal, while the album as a whole showed the band broadening beyond their earlier youthful swagger.\n\nThe album was well received and became another major UK success for the band, reaching number 3 on the UK Albums Chart and earning platinum certification. Released on Parlophone, it reinforced Supergrass’s reputation as one of the sharpest and most melodic British rock acts of the late 1990s, with a sound that combined wit, hook-heavy songwriting, and a tighter studio polish than their debut.",
